* linguist-vendored
*.js linguist-vendored=false
# Shell scripts must keep LF endings.  Several of these run on the Raspberry Pi
# (msxpi-tcpip-setup.sh) or under Git Bash / WSL, and CRLF breaks them outright
# - the shebang picks up a stray \r and the shell reports "bad interpreter" or
# "$'\r': command not found".  Windows tooling reintroduces CRLF very easily:
# Python's open(...,'w') translates \n to \r\n by default, which is exactly how
# these got broken once already.
*.sh        text eol=lf
software/build text eol=lf

# INL.CFG is read by InterNestor Lite on the MSX and must be CRLF.  With LF
# only, INL never finds a line boundary in it, reports "Cannot execute this
# command from a configuration file" and then loops printing its banner - which
# looks exactly like a hang in the UNAPI driver underneath.  build.sh converts
# it on copy as well, belt and braces.
*.CFG       text eol=crlf
